  "title": "Ends supply open distinctions that the knot test cannot tell from loops, and the law decides which a system has",
  "subject": "Where the open distinctions of infinite constraint systems come from",
  "conclusion": "In infinite parity systems an open distinction comes from a finite loop or from the ends; the 3-regular tree has a K1-K3 knot at every vertex without any loop, and no finite part or knot verdict tells the sources apart. The law decides the source: on the square grid Tseitin's vertex law has only loop-supplied openness, while Ledrappier's triangle law has no finite loop and every triangle is a knot opened by infinity.",
